===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# Directly [[overhead]]; vertically on top of. {{defdate|first attested before 1150.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|title=The climate of Tibet: Pole-land
|date=2013-05-11|volume=407|issue=8835|page=80
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21577341-worlds-third-largest-area-ice-about-undergo-systematic
|passage=Of all the transitions brought about on the Earth’s surface by temperature change, the melting of ice into water is the starkest. It is binary. And for the land beneath, the air '''above''' and the life around, it changes everything.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180217084317/https://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21577341-worlds-third-largest-area-ice-about-undergo-systematic|archivedate=17 February 2018}}
# Higher in the same page; earlier in the order as far as writing products go. {{defdate|first attested before 1150.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Present at a Hanging and Other Ghost Stories|year=1913|author=w:Ambrose Bierce|passage=Nobody has lived in it since the summer of 1879, and it is fast going to pieces. For some three years before the date mentioned '''above''', it was occupied by the family of Charles May}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Emanuel Swedenborg|title=Heaven and Hell|chapter=19|year=1905|passage=That angels are men in the most complete form, and enjoy every sense, may be seen above (n. 73-77); and that the light in heaven is far brighter than the light in the world (n. 126-132).}}
# Into or from heaven; in the sky. {{defdate|first attested around 1150–1350}}
#: {{ux|en|He’s in a better place now, floating free as the clouds '''above'''.}}
# In a higher place; upstairs; farther upstream. {{defdate|first attested around 1150–1350}}
# Higher in rank, power, or position. {{defdate|first attested around 1150–1350}}
#: {{ux|en|He appealed to the court '''above'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} In [[addition]]. {{defdate|first attested around 1150–1350}}
# More in number. {{defdate|first attested around 1350–1470}}
# Above zero; above freezing. {{defdate|first attested in the mid 20<sup>th</sup> century.}}
#: {{ux|en|It was a cold day at only 5 '''above'''.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} On the upper half or the [[dorsal]] surface of an animal.
#: {{ux|en|The sparrow I saw was rufous '''above''' and off-white below.}}

