==English==
[[File:Monitor Lizard.jpg|right|thumb|A '''monitor''' lizard]]
[[Image:Monitor LG.jpg|right|thumb|A CRT computer '''monitor''']]
[[File:HMSMarshalNeyUnderwayPortsideView1915.jpg|right|thumb|HMS ''Marshal Ney'', a '''monitor''' (warship)]]
[[File:Co monitor.JPG|right|thumb|A blood oxygen saturation '''monitor''']]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|monitour}} {{qualifier|obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*men-|id=think}}
From {{uder|en|la|monitor||warner}}, from perfect passive participle {{m|la|monitus||warning}}, from verb {{m|la|monere||to warn, admonish, remind}}.  Warship sense is from {{w|USS Monitor|USS ''Monitor''}}, the first ship of this type.

