##* {{quote-av|en|year=1997|role=w:Silent Bob|writer=w:Kevin Smith|title=w:Chasing Amy|passage=She was the girl, I know that now. But I pushed her away. So, I've spent every day since then '''chasing''' Amy… so to speak.}}
##* {{quote-song|en|title=w:Call Me Maybe|artist=w:Carly Rae Jepsen|year=2011|passage=But here's my number, so call me, maybe / And all the other boys try to '''chase''' me}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To [[pursue]] a [[vessel]] in order to [[destroy]], [[capture]] or [[interrogate]] her.
## {{lb|en|Hong Kong|Malaysia|colloquial}} To [[pressure]] another person; to [[nag]]
##: {{ux|en|I am not '''chasing''' you, I am asking you to do it professionally!}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To consume another beverage immediately after drinking [[hard liquor]], typically something better tasting or less harsh such as soda or beer; to use a drink as a [[chaser]].
#: {{ux|en|I need something to '''chase''' this shot with.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|title=In The Life: A Black Gay Anthology|editor=Joseph Beam|chapter=Brother to Brother: Words from the Heart|author=Joseph Beam|page=240|text=[He] '''chases''' his bedtime Valium with Johnny Walker Red.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:John Fogerty|title=Fortunate Son|year=2015|publisher=Little, Brown and Company|location=New York |page=401|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/fortunatesonmyli0000foge_c2k8/page/401/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-316-24457-2|passage=John ordered quite a few drinks. I think I stopped at four. He kept ordering straight shots of tequila and '''chasing''' them with a beer. Then he’d tear off the filter on his cigarette before smoking it.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|cricket}} To [[attempt]] to [[win]] by scoring the required number of runs in the final [[innings]].
#: {{ux|en|Australia will be '''chasing''' 217 for victory on the final day.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|baseball}} To swing at a [[pitch]] outside of the [[strike zone]], typically an outside pitch.
#: {{ux|en|Jones '''chases''' one out of the [[zone]] for strike two.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|baseball}} To produce enough [[offense]] to cause the [[pitcher]] to be removed.
#: {{ux|en|The rally '''chased''' the starter.}}

