spend.content:
==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:spenden|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|spenden}}, from {{inh|en|ang|spendan}} (attested especially in compounds {{m|ang|āspendan||to spend}}, {{m|ang|forspendan||to use up, consume}}), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*spendōn|t=to spend}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|expendere||to weigh out}}. {{doublet|en|expend}}.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|spentōn||to consume, use, spend}} (whence {{cog|de|spenden||to donate, provide}}), {{cog|dum|-}} {{m|nl|spenden||to spend, dedicate}}, Old {{cog|is|spenna||to spend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/spɛnd/|a=RP,GA,CA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-spend.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/spɪnd/|a=US,pin-pen}}
* {{IPA|en|/spend/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛnd|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|~s|~ing|spent}}

# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[pay out]] (money).
#: {{syn|en|outlay}}
#: {{ux|en|I've already '''spent''' hundreds of dollars buying dog chow.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''spends''' far more on gambling than he does on living proper.}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=1|passage=Then there came a reg'lar terror of a sou'wester same as you don't get one summer in a thousand, and blowed the shanty flat and ripped about half of the weir poles out of the sand. We '''spent''' consider'ble money getting 'em reset, and then a swordfish got into the pound and tore the nets all to slathers, right in the middle of the squiteague season.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=2013-05-25|volume=407|issue=8837|page=74
|title=No hiding place
|url=http://www.economist.com/news/science-and-technology/21578357-plan-assess-peoples-personal-characteristics-their-twitter-streams-no
|passage=In America alone, people '''spent''' $170 billion on “direct marketing”—junk mail of both the physical and electronic varieties—last year. Yet of those who received unsolicited adverts through the post, only 3% bought anything as a result.}}
# To bestow; to employ; often with ''on'' or ''upon''.
#* {{RQ:Herbert Temple
|passage=I {{...}} am never loath / To '''spend''' my judgment.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} To [[squander]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''spend''' an estate in gambling}}
# To [[exhaust]], to [[wear out]].
#: {{ux|en|The violence of the waves was '''spent'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Knolles Turkes
|passage=their bodies '''spent''' with long labour and thirst}}
# {{sid|en|time}} To [[consume]], to [[use up]] (time).
#: {{ux|en|My sister usually '''spends''' her free time in nightclubs.}}
#: {{ux|en|We '''spent''' the winter in the south of France.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1661|author={{w|John Fell (bishop)|John Fell}}|title=The Life of the most learned, reverend and pious Dr. H. Hammond|url=http://archive.org/stream/a615775104worduoft/a615775104worduoft_djvu.txt
|passage=During the whole time of his abode in the university he generally '''spent''' thirteen hours of the day in study; by which assiduity besides an exact dispatch of the whole course of philosophy, he read over in a manner all classic authors that are extant{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1945|month=September and October|author=C. Hamilton Ellis|title=Royal Trains—V|journal=Railway Magazine|page=251|text=The last occasion on which the Kaiser [Wilhelm II] used this train was for an inglorious journey into Holland towards the end of the 1914 war. He '''spent''' the night in it at Eysden [{{l|en|Eijsden}}], while the Queen of the Netherlands and a hastily summoned Cabinet debated what to do with him.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=w:Henry Petroski| title=Geothermal Energy|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/geothermal-energy| volume=101| issue=4| magazine=w:American Scientist| passage=Energy has seldom been found where we need it when we want it. Ancient nomads, wishing to ward off the evening chill and enjoy a meal around a campfire, had to collect wood and then '''spend''' time and effort coaxing the heat of friction out from between sticks to kindle a flame.}}
#* {{see more citations|en}}
# {{lb|en|dated|ambitransitive}} To have an [[orgasm]]; to [[ejaculate]] sexually.
#: {{ux|en|The fish '''spends''' his semen on eggs which he finds floating and whose mother he has never seen.}} <!--unsure of author: Ezra Pound??-->
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[waste]] or [[wear]] away; to be [[consume]]d.
#: {{ux|en|Energy '''spends''' in the using of it.}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=The sound '''spendeth''' and is dissipated in the open air.}}
# To be [[diffuse]]d; to [[spread]].
#* {{RQ:Bacon Sylva Sylvarum|passage=The vines that they use for wine are so often cut, that their sap '''spendeth''' into the grapes.}}
# {{lb|en|mining}} To [[break ground]]; to continue working.

