===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To suggest (that someone ought to do something, or that something ought to be the case) by, or as if by, using the word ''should''.
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2008-11-01|author=Damon L. Jacobs|title=Absolutely Should-Less: The Secret to Living the Stress-Free Life You Deserve|publisher=Morgan James Publishing|isbn=9781614484028
|text=I'd prefer that she stop '''shoulding''' me. I prefer that I stop '''shoulding''' me. I prefer that I stop '''shoulding''' her.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2015-03-08|author=Diane Brandon|title=Dream Interpretation for Beginners: Understand the Wisdom of Your Sleeping Mind|publisher=Llewellyn Worldwide|isbn=9780738743738
|text={{...}} for her to be kind to herself and less susceptible to others '''shoulding''' her. }}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that ought to be the case as opposed to already being the case.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1996|author=Fred Shoemaker|title=Extraordinary Golf: The Art of the Possible|page=88
|passage=When the golf ball is there, the whole self-interference package — the hopes, worries, and fears; the thoughts on how-to and how-not-to; the woulds, the coulds, and the '''shoulds''' — is there too.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=Overcoming Resistance in Cognitive Therapy|author=Robert L. Leahy
|passage=However, we can address maladaptive '''shoulds''' by examining the differences between prior events, causes, proximate causes, and moral responsibility.
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=NShtFzMDJckC&lpg=PA139&dq=%22shoulds%22&pg=PA159#v=onepage&q=%22shoulds%22&f=false}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2008|journal=Working Mother|volume=31|issue=8|page=20
|passage=Being a list-o-maniac, I suggested we make a list of the "'''shoulds'''" and "shouldn'ts." So in the darkness of hazy sleep, I began to mentally prepare mine. The first item on the "'''should'''" side was easy: a sibling for our 3-year-old daughter.}}

