===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[in|In]] an [[uncertain]] or [[unspecified]] [[location]].
#: {{ux|en|I must have left my glasses '''somewhere'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I've hidden candy '''somewhere''' in this room.}}
# [[to|To]] an uncertain or unspecified location.
#: {{ux|en|He plans to go '''somewhere''' warm for his vacation.}}
#: {{ux|en|I have to go '''somewhere''' at lunch. Can I meet you at 2?}}
# At some unspecified point.
#: {{ux|en|I don't remember the exact number, but it was '''somewhere''' between 200 and 300.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=1957 September|author=M. D. Greville and G. O. Holt|title=Railway Development in Manchester—1|journal=Railway Magazine|page=620, from [[Herapath]]'s Journal|text=When a train has to ascend the incline, it first runs down, engine first, from the station about 60 or 70 yards. Then comes behind it the aforesaid truck, or one similar, which, being attached to an endless wire rope, a communication is made by means of the electric telegraph to the engineman at the top of the incline, when the fixed engine begins to work, and the train, partly pulled by the locomotive before, and partly pushed by the truck behind, rapidly ascends, taking '''somewhere''' about three minutes to get up.}}

====Synonyms====
