====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Physical appendage.''
## A small [[label]].
##: {{syn|en|ticket}}
##: {{ux|en| He has a '''tag''' hung on his bag.}}
## A [[skin tag]], an [[excrescence]] of skin.
## A dangling lock of sheep's wool, matted with dung; a [[dung tag]].
## Any slight appendage, as to an article of dress; something slight hanging loosely.
## A metallic binding, tube, or point, at the end of a string, or lace, to stiffen it.
## {{lb|en|biochemistry}} Any short peptide sequence artificially attached to proteins mostly in order to help purify, solubilize or visualize these proteins.
## Something mean and paltry; rabble.
##* {{RQ:Spenser Ireland|passage=For upon the like Proclamation there, they all came in, both '''tag''' and rag}}
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Last nonphysical appendage.''
## {{senseid|en|music_appendage}} The last line (or last two lines) of a [[song]]'s [[chorus]] that is repeated to indicate the end of the song.
## {{lb|en|television}} The last scene of a TV program, often focusing on the program's [[subplot]].
##: {{antonyms|en|cold open}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Stephen V. Duncan|title=A Guide to Screenwriting Success|page=300|passage=Often, the '''tag''' punctuates the "we're all in this together" theme and is topped with a laugh.}}
## The end, or [[catchword]], of an actor's speech; [[cue]].
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Nonphysical label.''
## {{lb|en|informal|authorship}} An attribution in narrated dialogue (eg, "he said") or attributed words (e.g. "he thought").
##: {{syn|en|dialogue tag|speech tag|tag line}}
##* {{quote-newsgroup|en|passage=Seems here like Russ would be speaking. You could use a '''tag '''here.|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!search/dialogue$20tag$20-%22dialogue$20tag%22$20fiction/alt.fiction.original/ILKqK-v2aOo/LYrApsOirD4J|author=michael|newsgroup=alt.fiction.original}}
##* {{quote-newsgroup|en|passage=If you want to start with talk, stick a '''tag''' in right away|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!search/dialogue$20tag$20-%22dialogue$20tag%22$20fiction/alt.fiction.original/SmupYFqmvVg/J86TlRdrzS0J|author=Jane MacDonald|newsgroup=alt.fiction.original}}
##* {{quote-newsgroup|en|passage=You could combine these two paragraphs, I think, and rewrite to lose the '''tag''' portion of the third sentence.|url=https://groups.google.com/forum/#!search/dialogue$20tag$20-%22dialogue$20tag%22$20fiction/alt.fiction.original/srDkU_1xqVM/SAP8ITOS9gkJ|author=bart_...@hotmail.com|newsgroup=alt.fiction.original}}
## {{lb|en|computing}} A piece of [[markup]] representing an [[element]] in a [[markup language]].
##: {{ux|en|The <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> '''tag''' provides a title for the Web page.}}
##: {{ux|en|The <code>&lt;sarcasm&gt;</code> '''tag''' conveys sarcasm in Internet slang.}}
## {{senseid|en|keyword}} {{lb|en|computing}} A [[keyword]], term, or phrase associated with or assigned to data, media, and/or information enabling keyword-based [[classification]]; often used to categorize content.
##: {{ux|en|I want to add genre and artist '''tags''' to the files in my music collection.}}
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Identity.''
## {{lb|en|chiefly|US}} A [[vehicle]] [[number]] plate; a medal bearing identification data (animals, soldiers).
##: {{usex|en|The subwoofer in the trunk was so loud, it vibrated the '''tag''' like an aluminum can.}}
## {{lb|en|slang}} A person's [[name]].
##: {{ux|en|What’s your '''tag'''?}}
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Involving being tagged physically.''
## {{senseid|en|game of chasing and labeling}} {{lb|en|uncountable|children's game}} A game, especially for children on [[playground]]s, in which one player (known as "it") attempts to touch another, who then becomes "it"; any similar game of chasing and trying to reach, touch, shoot, or label other players.
##: {{syn|en|tips|q1=Australia|it|q2=UK}}
##: {{hypo|en|archery tag|dart tag|freeze tag|hoop scoot tag|laser tag|sardines|zombie tag}}
## {{lb|en|baseball}} An instance of touching the [[baserunner]] with the [[ball]] or the ball in a gloved hand to rule him "out."
##: {{ux|en|The '''tag''' was applied at second for the final out.}}
# {{lb|en|heading}} ''Signature.''
## {{lb|en|graffiti slang}} [[graffiti|Graffiti]] in the form of a stylized signature particular to the artist.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Scape Martinez|title=Graff 2: Next Level Graffiti Techniques|page=124|passage=There is a hierarchy of sorts: a throw-up can go over a '''tag''', a piece over a throw-up, and a burner over a piece.}}
# A type of [[cardboard]].
# A [[sheep]] in its first year.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1807|title=The Complete Farmer, or, General Dictionary of Agriculture and Husbandry|oclc=779076327|passage=After being weaned, the ram or wedder lamb is sometimes termed ''hog'', ''hoggit'', or '''''tag''''', during the whole of the first year}}

