alone.content:
==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:allone|:afeq|all|one|:afeq|al-|one|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|allone}}, from earlier {{m|enm|[[all]] [[oon]]|lit=all one}}, contracted from the {{der|en|ang|-}} phrase {{m|ang|[[eall]] [[ān]]|t=completely alone}}, equivalent to {{af|en|al-<t:all>|one|nocat=1}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|alane|t=alone}}, {{cog|stq|alleene|t=alone}}, {{cog|fy|allinne|t=alone}}, {{cog|nl|alleen|t=alone}}, {{cog|nds|alleen|t=alone}}, {{cog|de|allein|t=alone}}, {{cog|da|alene|t=alone}}, {{cog|sv|allena|t=alone}}. More at {{l|en|all}} and {{l|en|one}}. For the different phonological development of {{m|en||alone}} and {{m|en||one}}, see the note in {{m|en|one}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ə-lōnʹ}}
* {{a|en|UK}}
** {{IPA|en|/əˈləʊn/|a=RP}}
** {{IPA|en|/əˈlɛːn/|a=Northumbria}}
** {{IPA|en|/əˈlon/|a=Scotland}}
** {{IPA|en|/əˈloːn/|a=Wales,non-toe-tow}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈloʊn/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˈlʌon/|a=Dublin}}
* {{IPA|en|/aˈluŋ/|a=Hong Kong}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-alone.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-alone.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊn|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|a|lone}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}} {{tlb|en|predicative|_|only}}

# [[by oneself|By oneself]], [[solitary]].
#: {{syn|en|on one's own|unaccompanied}}
#: {{ux|en|I can't ask for help because I am '''alone'''.}}
## Not involved in a [[romantic]] relationship.
##: {{syn|en|available|single|unattached|unpartnered}}
##: {{hypo|en|unmarried}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Genesis|ii|18|text=It is not good that the man should be '''alone'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1798|author=w:Samuel Taylor Coleridge|title=w:The Rime of the Ancient Mariner
|passage='''Alone''' on a wide, wide sea.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|title=Who Is Cilia Flores? What to Know About Maduro’s Wife Amid Fall of Venezuela's First Couple|date=Jan 5 2026|author=Callum Sutherland|text=When Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro was captured by U.S. special forces during a historic raid in his native homeland, he wasn't '''alone'''. His wife, Cilia Flores, was also detained.|url=https://time.com/7343188/who-is-cilia-flores-maduro-wife-venezuela-politics/|accessdate=6 January 2026|archiveurl=https://ghostarchive.org/archive/20260223000228/https://time.com/7343188/who-is-cilia-flores-maduro-wife-venezuela-politics/|archivedate=23 February 2026}}
# {{lb|en|predicatively|chiefly in the negative}} Lacking [[peer]]s who share one's beliefs, experiences, practices, etc.
#: {{syn|en|deserted|forsaken|isolated}}
#: {{ux|en|Senator Craddock wants to abolish the estate tax, and she's not '''alone'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I always organize my Halloween candy before eating it. Am I '''alone''' in this?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-23|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/iantraynor Ian Traynor]| volume=189| issue=11| page=1| magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly| url=http://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/aug/13/eastern-europe-autocrats-return-test-democracy|title=Eastern European autocrats pose new test for democracy| passage=Hungary's leader is not '''alone''' in eastern and southern Europe, where democratically elected populist strongmen increasingly dominate, deploying the power of the state and a battery of instruments of intimidation to crush dissent, demonise opposition, tame the media and tailor the system to their ends.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230517082630/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2013/aug/13/eastern-europe-autocrats-return-test-democracy}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021-09-08|author=Ekua Hagan|magazine=w:Psychology Today|url=https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/blog/your-personal-renaissance/202109/5-ways-restore-our-hope|title=5 Ways to Restore Our Hope|passage = If you’ve been feeling overwhelmed by it all, you’re not '''alone'''.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Apart from, or exclusive of, others.
#: {{syn|en|exclusive|sole}}
#* {{RQ:Olivier Discourse of Women|page=18
|text=There are proofs enough in History, and first that beautiful ''Hynes'', so much beloved by ''Charles'' the seventh King of ''France'', who valued the '''alone''' possession of her Love at so high a rate, that{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Bentley Confutation of Atheism|passage=God, {{...}} by whose '''alone''' power and conversation we all live, and move, and have our being.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[mere|Mere]]; consisting of nothing further.
#: {{syn|en|simple|only|very|Thesaurus:mere}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1676|author=w:Robert Barclay|title=An Apology for the True Christian Divinity{{...}}
|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=ozEVAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA13
|text=and therefore all Killing, Banishing, Fining, Imprisoning, and other such things, which Men are afflicted with, for the '''alone''' exercise of their Conscience, or difference in Worship or Opinion, proceedeth from the spirit of ''Cain'', the Murderer, and is contrary to the Truth;
}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[unique|Unique]]; [[rare]]; [[matchless]].
#: {{syn|en|nonpareil|peerless|unparalleled|Thesaurus:unique}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=c. 1589–1593| author=w:William Shakespeare| title=w:The Two Gentlemen of Verona| section=act 2, scene 4| lines=163–165| passage=Pardon me, Proteus, all I can is nothing / To her, whose worth makes other worthies nothing; / She is '''alone'''.}}

