#* {{RQ:Conrad Heart of Darkness|page=209|passage=In the steady '''buzz''' of flies the homeward-bound agent was lying flushed and insensible[.]}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Ripley's Unbelievable Stories For Guys|author=Ripley's Believe It Or Not! (compiler)|page=|passage=This probably explains the interest in UVB-76, or “The Buzzer,” a mysterious shortwave radio station that has been operating since 1982 and whose output consists of a monotonous '''buzz''' repeated 24 hours a day, occasionally interrupted by a Russian voice.}}
# A [[whisper]].
# The [[audible]] [[friction]] of voiced [[consonant]]s.
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[rush]] or [[feeling]] of [[energy]] or [[excitement]]; a [[feeling]] of [[slight]] [[intoxication]].
#: {{ux|en|Still feeling the '''buzz''' from the coffee, he pushed through the last of the homework.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} A [[telephone call]] or e-mail.
