==English==
{{Wiktionary:Picture dictionary/en:head}}
{{wp}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=bodypart|:inh|enm:nekke|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|nekke}}, {{m|enm|nakke}}, from {{inh|en|ang|hnecca}}, {{m|ang|*hnæcca|t=neck, nape}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hnakkō}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hnakkô|t=nape, neck}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*knog-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kneg-|t=back of the head, nape, neck}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|sco|nek|t=neck}}, {{cog|frr|neek}}, {{m|frr|neeke}}, {{m|frr|Nak|t=neck}}, {{cog|stq|Näkke|t=neck}}, {{cog|fy|nekke|t=neck}}, {{cog|nl|nek|t=neck}}, {{cog|nds-de|Nack|t=neck}}, {{cog|de|Nacken|t=nape of the neck}}, {{cog|da|nakke|t=neck}}, {{cog|sv|nacke|t=nape of the neck}}, {{cog|is|hnakki|t=neck}}, {{cog|xto|kñuk|t=neck, nape}}. Possibly a mutated variant of *''kneug/k'' (compare {{cog|ang|hnocc|t=hook, penis}}, {{cog|cy|cnwch|t=joint, knob}}, {{cog|lv|knaūķis|t=dwarf}}. {{doublet|en|nek}}. More at {{m|en|nook}}. Displaced {{m|en|halse|t=neck, throat}} and {{m|en|swire|t=neck}}.

[[File:Structure of Adam's apple.png|right|thumb|A human neck.]]

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|en|/nɛk/|a=RP,US,CA}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-neck.wav|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-neck.ogg|a=US}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-neck.wav|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/nek/|a=AU,NZ}}
** {{IPA|en|[nek]|~|[ne̞k]|a=AU}}
** {{IPA|en|[ne̝k]|~|[nɪk]|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛk|s=1}}
* {{hyph|en|neck}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}
[[File:Anhinga novaehollandiae neck.jpg|thumb|right|An Australasian Darter extends her long neck.]]

# {{sid|en|Q9633}}{{lb|en|anatomy}} The part of the [[body]] connecting the [[head]] and the [[trunk]] found in humans and some animals.
#: {{syn|en|scrag}} 
#: {{ux|en|Giraffes have long '''necks'''.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|OCLC=1154662802|developer=[[w:ZA/UM|ZA/UM]]|title=Disco Elysium|date=15 October 2019|author2=[[w:Robert Kurvitz|Robert Kurvitz]]|quotee=You|text=Mother, help me, there's a head attached to my '''neck''' and I'm ''in'' it.}}
# The corresponding part in some other anatomical contexts.
# The part of a [[shirt]], [[dress]] etc., which fits a person's '''neck'''.
# The [[taper]]ed part of a [[bottle]] toward the opening.
# {{lb|en|botany}} The slender tubelike [[extension]] atop an [[archegonium]], through which the [[sperm]] swim to reach the [[egg]].
#* {{RQ:Schuster Hepaticae|volume=V|page=5|text=Archegonia are surrounded early in their development by the juvenile perianth, through the slender beak of which the elongated '''neck''' of the fertilized archegonium protrudes.}}
# {{lb|en|music}} The [[extension]] of any [[stringed]] [[instrument]] on which a [[fingerboard]] is mounted
# A long narrow [[tract]] of [[land]] projecting from the main body, or a narrow tract connecting two larger tracts.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A reduction in size near the end of an object, formed by a [[groove]] around it.
#: {{uxi|en|a '''neck''' forming the journal of a shaft}}
# The [[constriction]] between the [[root]] and [[crown]] of a [[tooth]].
# {{lb|en|architecture}} The [[gorgerin]] of a [[capital]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} A {{pedlink|volcanic plug}}, solidified lava filling the vent of an extinct volcano.
# {{lb|en|firearms}} The small part of a [[gun]] between the [[chase]] and the [[swell]] of the [[muzzle]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A person's [[life]].
#: {{co|en|to risk one's '''neck'''; to save someone's '''neck'''}}
# {{lb|en|informal|MLE|slang}} A [[falsehood]]; a [[lie]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[fellatio|Fellatio]]
#: {{syn|en|Kirk}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2016|artist=Smino|title=Pimptations|text=Shorty throw '''neck''' like a geese<br>She make me speak Portuguese}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2018|artist=Pouya|album=The South Got Something To Say|title=Florida Thang|text=She drop '''neck''' for a check and a paystub}}
# {{lb|en|now|historical}} A bundle of wheat used in certain English harvest ceremonies.
#* {{quote-book|en|author=R. A. R.|title=The Everyday Book|year=1837|page=1169|text=The person with 'the '''neck'''' stands in the centre, grasping it with both his hands}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James George Frazer|title=The Golden Bough|year=1911|volume=7|page=266|text="The '''neck'''" is generally hung up in the farmhouse, where it remains for two or three years.}}

