===Etymology===
From English dialectal {{m|en|hyke||to walk vigorously}}, probably a Northern form of {{m|en|hitch}}, from {{inh|en|enm|hytchen}}, {{m|enm|hichen}}, {{m|enm|icchen||to move, jerk, stir}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|hyke||to move with a jerk}}, dialectal {{cog|de|hicken||to hobble, walk with a limp}}, {{cog|da|hinke||to hop}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/haɪk/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-hike.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪk|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|haik|qq=one pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{wikidata lexeme|L16918}}
{{en-noun}}

# A long walk, usually for pleasure or exercise. {{defdate|from c. 1900}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|journal=Bulletin of the Cooper Ornithological Club| volume=1-6| page=149| year=1904| publisher=Cooper Ornithological Club| title=Extracts from Some Montana Note-books, 1904| author=P.M. Silloway| passage=Well, if it gave him so much pleasure to find the nest, he is welcome to the eggs. I can hunt another grass tuft, lay another set, and rear my brood in peace while he goes "'''hiking'''" after eggs at Flathead.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=California Parks Access: A Complete Guide to the State and National Parks for Visitors with Limited Mobility| author=Allen Mitchell| year=1992| page=179| passage=From here, you can pick up the asphalt bike path and take a '''hike''' across the meadow.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The 55 Best Places to '''Hike''' with Your Dog in the Philadelphia Region| author=Doug Gelbert| year=2002| page=98| passage=The '''hike''' along the trolley line from Smedley to Thompson Park is a wild and wooly excursion that brings you across train tracks, through dry creek beds, past ferns and wild roses and more.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Hiking California's Wine Country: A Guide to the Area's Greatest '''Hikes'''| page=166| author=Bubba Suess| year=2015| passage=The '''hike''' through the city of Napa's Alston Park is a great introduction to the Napa Valley.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Best Hikes Cleveland: The Greatest Views, Wildlife, and Forest Strolls|page=75| author=Joe Baur| year=2019| passage=You'll run into Powers Road and will '''hike''' on the sidewalks of Bedford across some train tracks and onto Broadway Avenue.}}
# An abrupt increase.
#: {{ant|en|cut<qq:used in same context>|decrease}}
#: {{ux|en|The tenants were not happy with the rent '''hike'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=25 Dec 76|volume=4|number=26|journal=Gay Community News|page=10|author=Alan Bowne|title=Lesbians Rising Makes an Impact at Hunter|text=It was on this campus last winter that gay people stood in the vanguard of protests against a tuition '''hike''' proposed and passed during the city's fiscal crisis.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 October 20|title=Network News: How do operators buy electricity?|journal=RAIL|issue=942|page=7|text=Those who are part of the consortium are protected from the current energy price '''hikes''' because they were tied into a fixed rate deal set almost a year ago (and continuing into most of next year).}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/15/interest-rate-us-latest-increase-federal-reserve|title=Federal Reserve announces biggest interest rate hike since 1994|date=2022-06-15|author=Dominic Rushe|passage=With soaring inflation and the shadow of recession hanging over the United States, the Federal Reserve announced a 0.75 percentage-point increase in interest rates on Wednesday – the largest '''hike''' since 1994.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261024005221/https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/jun/15/interest-rate-us-latest-increase-federal-reserve|archivedate=24 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|American football}} The [[snap]] of the ball to start a play.
# A sharp upward tug to raise something.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=Erik Schubach|title=The Hollow
|passage=She gave a cute '''hike''' of her skirt as she spun and almost sauntered down the stairs.}}

