destroy.content:
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*strew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|destroyen}}, from {{der|en|fro|destruire}}, {{der|en|la-vul|*destrugō}}, from Classical {{der|en|la|dēstruō}}, from {{m|la|dē-|t=un-, de-}} + {{m|la|struō|t=to build}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈstɹɔɪ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-destroy.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-destroy.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪ|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|de|stroy}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{senseid|en|v1}}{{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[damage]] beyond [[use]] or [[repair]]; to damage (something) to the point that it effectively ceases to exist.
#: {{ux|en|The earthquake '''destroyed''' several apartment complexes.}}
#: {{ux|en|Hooligans '''destroy''' unprovoked.}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|John|2|19|passage=Iesus answered, and said vnto them, '''Destroy''' this temple, and in three dayes I will raise it vp.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Joan Lee Faust|title=AROUND THE Garden|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1972/11/05/archives/around-the-garden.html|date=1972-11-05|passage=Repeated use of this type of [water] on plants results in deflocculation[] of the soil. Good quality soil consists of loose aggregates which provide natural aeration and ease of root run. Sodium accumulation in soil '''destroys''' this natural flocculation and causes the soil to pack.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20241203143400/https://www.nytimes.com/1972/11/05/archives/around-the-garden.html}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Steven McLaughlin|title=Clubland UK: On the Door in the Rave Era
|passage=Krav is a martial art of last resort that assumes no quarter and focuses purely on disarming, disabling and, if necessary, '''destroying''' your opponent.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Jill Filipovic|title=Opinion: Elon Musk’s Israel tour was transparently transactional and insulting|url=https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/28/opinions/elon-musk-israel-tour-antisemitism-filipovic/index.html|date=2023-11-28|passage=Musk’s Israel tour was transparently transactional and frankly insulting. The antisemitic sentiment Musk endorsed had nothing to do with Israel; “replacement theory” is generally an unsupported allegation that Jews and other immigrants in the US and Europe are '''destroying''' Western civilization.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20231202141134/https://www.cnn.com/2023/11/28/opinions/elon-musk-israel-tour-antisemitism-filipovic/index.html}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[neutralize]], undo a [[property]] or [[condition]].
#: {{ux|en|Smoking '''destroys''' the natural subtlety of the palate.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[put down]] or [[euthanize]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Destroying''' a rabid dog is required by law.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To severely disrupt the well-being of (a person); [[ruin]].
#: {{ux|en|Her divorce '''destroyed''' her; she had a nervous breakdown and was severely depressed for more than a year.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2005|title=Kliatt Young Adult Paperback Book Guide
|passage=Other girls in the foster home are eager to '''destroy''' her and get her kicked out of the place. It's a tough situation.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} To utterly [[defeat]]; to [[crush#Verb|crush]].
#: {{ux|en|Remember when Germany '''destroyed''' Brazil 7–1 in the World Cup?}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410211749/https://www.nytimes.com/2012/11/11/magazine/the-oklahoma-city-thunders-fairy-tale-rise.html|author=Sam Anderson|authorlink=Sam Anderson (writer)|title=The Oklahoma City Thunder's Fairy-Tale Rise|date=11 November 2012|passage=Growing up, [[w:Kevin Durant|&#91;Kevin&#93; Durant]] told me, he was a sore loser. That all changed one day when he was 11, after he got '''destroyed''' by his father in a game of one on one in the driveway.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To [[remove]] [[data]].
#: {{ux|en|The memory leak happened because we forgot to '''destroy''' the temporary lists.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|bodybuilding|slang|antiphrasis}} To [[exhaust]] completely and thus [[recreate]] or [[build up]].
#: {{ux|en|This exercise is going to '''destroy''' all parts of your shoulders.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang|vulgar}} To penetrate sexually in an aggressive way.
#: {{ux|en|She got '''destroyed''' by her lover on the carpet.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|US|slang}} To [[sing]] a [[song]] extremely poorly.
#* {{quote-av|en|title=Rush Hour 2|publisher=New Line Cinema|author=Jeff Nathanson|year=2001|passage=JAMES CARTER: The man's '''destroying''' a classic!|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OfORiypbhkg}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To eat food [[quickly]], [[hungrily]] or [[completely]].
#: {{ux|en|I could '''destroy''' some wings right now.}}

