===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[inflatable]] [[buoyant]] object, often (but not necessarily) [[round]] and [[flexible]].
# Such an object as a child’s [[toy]] or [[party]] [[decoration]].
# Such an object designed to [[transport]] people or equipment through the [[air]].
#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Jeffries; w:Jean-Pierre Blanchard|title=A narrative of the two aerial Voyages of Dr. J. with Mons. Blanchard: with meteorological observations and remarks.|url=https://books.google.co.nz/books?id=WztfAAAAcAAJ|year=1786|page=45|passage=We immediately threw out all the little things we had with us, ſuch as biſcuits, apples, &c. and after that one of our oars or wings; but ſtill deſcending, we caſt away the other wing, and then the [[governail]] ; having likewiſe had the precaution, for fear of accidents, while the '''Balloon''' was filling, partly to looſen and make it go eaſy, I now ſucceeded in attempting to reach without the Car, and unſcrewing the moulinet, with all its apparatus; I likewiſe caſt that into the ſea.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A [[sac]] inserted into part of the [[body]] for [[therapeutic]] reasons; such as [[angioplasty]].
# A [[speech bubble]].
# A wide rounded [[glass]] with a stem and foot, used for [[wine]], [[brandy]], etc.
#: {{syn|en|ballon|balloon glass}}
# {{lb|en|architecture}} A ball or globe on the top of a pillar, church, etc.
#: {{co|en|the '''balloon''' of St. Paul’s Cathedral in London}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[round]] [[vessel]], usually with a short [[neck]], to hold or receive whatever is [[distill]]ed; a glass vessel of a [[spherical]] form.
# {{lb|en|pyrotechnics}} A [[bomb]] or [[shell]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A game played with a large inflated ball.
# {{lb|en|engraving}} The [[outline]] enclosing words represented as coming from the mouth of a pictured [[figure]].
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[woman]]'s [[breast]].
#: {{synonyms|en|Thesaurus:breasts}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A small container for [[illicit]] drugs made from a condom or the finger of a latex glove, etc.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2016|author=David Cornwell|title=Like it Matters
|passage=And all I had to do in return was take a drive up to Ricardo's place on the way home and then a pretty edgy one back to Rondebosch with a '''balloon''' of coke sandwiched between two pairs of underpants.}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} {{synonym of|en|balloon payment}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1986|author=James M. Johnson|title=Fundamentals of finance for equipment lessors
|passage=The purpose of the '''balloon''' is to reduce the periodic payment required during the life of the financing period.}}

