##* {{quote-book|en|year=1964|author=U.S. Atomic Energy Commission|title=The Effects of Nuclear Weapons|page=417
|passage=The composition of the fallout can also be changed by "'''salting'''" the weapon to be detonated. This consists in the inclusion of significant quantities of certain elements, possibly enriched in specific isotopes, for the purpose of producing induced radioactivity. There are several reasons why a weapon might be '''salted'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[sprinkle]] [[throughout]].
#: {{ux|en|They '''salted''' the document with arcane language.}}
