{{also|recyclé}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:af|re-|cycle|text=+|tree=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌɹiːˈsaɪkəl/|[ˌɹiːˈsaɪkɫ̩]|/ˌɹɪˈsaɪkəl/|[ˌɹɪ̝ˈsaɪkɫ̩]|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recycle.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹəˈsaɪkəl/|/ɹɪˈsaɪkəl/|/ɹiˈsaɪkəl/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈsʌɪk(ə)l/|[ɹɪˈsəi̯k(ə)ɫ]|a=CA,Canadian raising}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪkəl|s=3}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[break down]] and [[reuse]] [[component]] [[material]]s.
#: {{ux|en|Both paper and plastic can be '''recycled'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2024 May 29|title=Network News: HS2's Bromford Tunnel portal complete ready for TBM breakthrough...|journal=RAIL|issue=1010|page=14|text='''Recycling''' and reusing the material eliminates the need to import aggregate, a strategy which has avoided over 50,000 lorry movements on local roads.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|figurative}} To [[reuse]] as a whole.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=12 July 2012|author=Sam Adams|work=AV Club|title=Ice Age: Continental Drift|passage=Jokes are '''recycled''' so frequently, it’s as if comedy writing was eating a hole in the ozone layer: If the audience had a nickel for every time a character on one side of the frame says something could never happen as it simultaneously happens on the other side of the frame, they’d have enough to pay the surcharge for the movie’s badly implemented 3-D.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Paul Rees|title=Finn Russell masterminds historic Scotland victory over England|url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2018/feb/24/scotland-england-six-nations-match-report|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180422092213/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2018/feb/24/scotland-england-six-nations-match-report|archivedate=22 April 2018|date=24 February 2018|passage=He &#91;[[w:Huw Jones (rugby union)|Huw Jones]]&#93; was hauled down in England’s 22 but, when the ball was quickly '''recycled''', [[w:Finn Russell|[Finn] Russell]]’s miss-pass gave {{w|Sean Maitland}} the room to score in the left corner.}}
#* {{RQ:FT|edition=weekend|author=Simon Kuper|date=2025-09-13|title=How Maga rewrote the Little Red Book|section=Life & Arts|page=18|passage=Now populists '''recycle''' communist verities: the fetishisation of working-class culture, the vision of a good “people” fighting a bad elite, the belief that the state should control business and the dismissal of parliamentary democracy as a bourgeois sham.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[collect]] or [[place]] in a [[bin]] for recycling.
#* '''1990''', Laurence Sombke, ''The Solution to Pollution: 101 Things You Can Do to Clean Up Your Environment'', Sandy, Oregon: MasterMedia, p 22:
#*: Most cans, bottles, and jars need to be rinsed, so '''recycle''' while you are doing dishes.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|title=The Complete Guide to Easy Woodworking Projects: 50 Projects You Can Build With Hand Power Tools|location=Minneapolis|publisher=Creative Publishing International|page=270
|passage='''Recycling''' is no longer a chore when this convenient '''recycling''' center is a fixture in your kitchen.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Elaine Martin Petrowski|title=Design Ideas for Home Storage|location=Upper Saddle River, New Jersey|publisher=Creative Homeowner|page=133
|passage=You'll find many configurations, including models that hide behind a single cabinet door and conceal from one to three bins, so you can '''recycle''' at the same spot where you dispose of trash.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|title=The greenest flags: virtue signals that help you find love – from patchwork clothes to car sharing|date=2026-03-02|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/mar/02/greenest-flags-virtue-signals-help-find-love-patchwork-clothes-car-sharing|passage=Who cares if you’re good-looking if you don’t '''recycle'''? Essentially, yes. Car-sharing, wearing patchwork clothes (signifying mending rather than throwing away) and carrying reusable coffee cups all came up as signs of environmentally virtuous behaviour.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261018134310/https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/mar/02/greenest-flags-virtue-signals-help-find-love-patchwork-clothes-car-sharing|archivedate=18 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|ergative}} To be recycled.
#: {{ux|en|Sulfur '''recycles''' in the sulfur cycle.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} To {{ll|en|discard}} into a recycling bin.
# {{lb|en|US|military|transitive}} To put (a person) through a course of training again.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Barbara Schading; Richard Schading|title=A Civilian's Guide to the U.S. Military|page=102
|passage=Recruits cannot fail this portion of their training and become a Marine. Anyone who fails may be “'''recycled'''” through training up to three more times to try again, but will be sent home if success in this program is not achieved.}}
# {{lb|en|roller derby}} To [[skate]] toward the rear of the engagement zone to maximize the time that an opposing [[jammer]] must spend before returning to the action.
