soil.content:
==English==
[[Image:Oklahoma state soil.JPG|thumb|right|'''Soil''' at varying depths.]]
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/sɔɪl/|[sɔɪ̯ɫ]}}
** {{IPA|en|/sɔɪ.əl/|[sɔi̯əɫ]|[sɔi̯l̩]|a=pre-l breaking}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-soil.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔɪl|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|soile}}, {{m|enm|soyle}}, {{m|enm|sule|t=ground, earth}}, partly from {{der|en|xno|soyl|t=bottom, ground, pavement}}, from {{der|en|la|solium|t=seat, chair; throne}}, mistaken for {{der|en|la|solum|t=ground, foundation, earth, sole of the foot}}; and partly from {{inh|en|ang|sol|t=mud, mire, wet sand}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sulą|t=mud, spot}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*sūl-|t=thick liquid}}. Cognate with {{cog|gml|söle|t=dirt, mud}}, {{cog|dum|sol|t=dirt, filth}}, {{cog|gmh|sol}}, {{m|gmh|söl|t=dirt, mud, mire}}, {{cog|da|søle|t=mud, muck}}. Compare {{cog|fr|seuil|t=level; threshold}} and {{m|fr|sol|t=soil, earth; ground}}. See also {{l|en|sole}}, {{l|en|soal}}, {{l|en|solum}}.

For the sole and soil relation, compare typologically {{m+|ru|по́чва}} akin to {{m|ru|подо́шва}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|soyl||obsolete}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} A mixture of [[mineral]] [[particle]]s and [[organic]] material, used to support plant growth.
#: {{ux|en|We bought a bag of '''soil''' for the houseplants.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The unconsolidated mineral or organic material on the immediate surface of the earth that serves as a natural medium for the growth of land plants.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The unconsolidated mineral or organic matter on the surface of the earth that has been subjected to and shows effects of genetic and environmental factors of: climate (including water and temperature effects), and macro- and microorganisms, conditioned by relief, acting on parent material over a period of time. A product-soil differs from the material from which it is derived in many physical, chemical, biological, and morphological properties and characteristics.
# Country or territory.
