===Verb===
{{en-verb|~s|biting|bit|bitten,bit}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cut]] into or [[press]] into (something) by [[clamp]]ing one's [[tooth|teeth]] (piercing or gripping it). {{q|Compare {{m|en|bite off||sever by biting}}.}}
#: {{cot|en|chew|gnaw|nip}}<!--cf., with the back teeth, to crush or grind-->
#: {{ux|en|As soon as you '''bite''' that sandwich, you'll know how good it is.}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't '''bite''' your nails.}}
#: {{ux|en|The bear '''bit''' the fish in two.}}<!-- {{q|Compare {{m|en|bite off}}.}}-->
# <!-- listed as a separate sense because it doesn't take an object direction, "bite X", like sense 1, but instead is "bite through X", etc: -->{{lb|en|intransitive|or with "through", "on", "into", "away at", etc}} To press the teeth into or clamp the teeth onto or around (something). {{q|Compare {{m|en|bite down}}.}}
#: {{ux|en|That dog is about to '''bite'''!}}
#: {{ux|en|After you '''bite''' through the bread — '''bite''' down into and past the bread — you'll reach the fillings.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Bite''' on this stick while the medic removes the spike from your leg. {{q|Or: {{m|en|bite down}} on this stick while [...]}} }}
#* '''1907''', Henry Taylor, "A Canine Idiosyncrasy", in "The British Veterinary Journal'', volume 63, page 26: 
#*: The {{...}} red-brown, Samoyede dog {{...}} would drop his hindquarters on the ground, {{...}} and '''bite''' away at the region of his thigh and tail, and pull out the hair in mouthfuls.
#* '''1914''', ''Songs and Verses for a Baby'', page 67:<!--ambiguous/unclear as to whether 'habitually' is part of what is meant-->
#*: Let dogs delight to bark and '''bite''' / For God hath made them so; / Let bears and lions growl and fight, / For 'tis their nature to.
## {{lb|en|in particular}} To have a habit of pressing the teeth into (and wounding) people, animals, etc.
##: {{ux|en|Be careful: that dog '''bites'''. Does your cat '''bite'''?}}<!--clearly shows the 'habitual' part of the definition, since all cats bite their food, but this is still a coherent question with the implied object 'people'-->
# {{lb|en|intransitive|chiefly|negative polarity}} To [[behave]] [[aggressive]]ly; to [[reject]] [[advance]]s.
#: {{ux|en|If you see me, come and say hello. I don't '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[take hold]]; to [[establish]] [[firm]] [[contact]] with.
#: {{ux|en|I needed snow chains to make the tires '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To have [[significant]] [[effect]], often [[negative]].
#: {{ux|en|For homeowners with adjustable rate mortgages, rising interest will really '''bite'''.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|of a fish}} To bite a [[bait]]ed [[hook]] or other [[lure]] and thus be [[catch|caught]].
#: {{ux|en|Are the fish '''biting''' today?}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|metaphor}} To [[accept]] something [[offer]]ed, often [[secret]]ly or [[deceptive]]ly, to cause some [[action]] by the [[acceptor]].
#: {{ux|en|I've planted the story. Do you think they'll '''bite'''?}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive|of an insect}} To [[sting]].{{rfv-sense|en}}
#: {{ux|en|These mosquitoes are really '''biting''' today!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author=James Joyce|title=Ulysses|chapter=Penelope|publisher=Shakespeare and Company|location=Paris|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/4300/pg4300-images.html|passage=Whit Monday is a cursed day too no wonder that bee '''bit''' him better the seaside}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1982|author=Raymond E. Fowler|title=The Andreasson Affair, Phase Two|publisher=Prentice-Hall|page=53|isbn=9780130366160|lccn=81021194|url=https://uncorruptedtruth.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/the-andreasson-affair-phase-two-1982.pdf|passage=I'm crying because the bee '''bit''' me. [...] I told her that the bee hit me and stung me right there.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=pattrice jones|chapter=Stomping with the Elephants: Feminist Principles for Radical Solidarity|title=Igniting a Revolution: Voices in Defense of the Earth|publisher=AK Press|page=330|isbn=9781904859567|lccn=2006920971|url=https://www.thetedkarchive.com/library/steven-best-and-anthony-j-nocella-igniting-a-revolution|passage=In the state of Louisiana, bees '''bit''' back when children threw rocks at their hive. [...] stings suffered by the aggressive children.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Alice Hoffman|title=The Dovekeepers|publisher=Scribner|isbn=9781451617481|url=https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/The-Dovekeepers/Alice-Hoffman/9781451617481|passage=When a wasp '''bit''' me and a red welt rose on my arm, [...] I burned from the sting of the wasp but insisted I was fine.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To cause a [[smart]]ing [[sensation]]; to have a [[property]] which causes such a sensation; to be [[pungent]].
#: {{ux|en|It '''bites''' like pepper or mustard.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|sometimes|figurative}} To cause [[sharp]] [[pain]] or [[damage]] to; to [[hurt]] or [[injure]].
#: {{ux|en|Pepper '''bites''' the mouth.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|V|ii|229|1|passage={{...}}froſts doe '''bite''' the Meads{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To cause sharp pain; to [[produce]] [[anguish]]; to hurt or injure; to have the property of so doing.
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Proverbs|23|32|column=1|url=https://archive.org/details/Bible1611/page/n741/mode/1up|text=At the laſt it [wine] '''biteth''' like a ſerpent, and ſtingeth like ‖ an adder.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[take]] or [[keep]] a [[firm]] [[hold]].
#: {{ux|en|The anchor '''bites'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[take hold]] of; to hold [[fast]]; to [[adhere]] to.
#: {{ux|en|The anchor '''bites''' the ground.}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Tale of Two Cities|Fire Rises|152|{{...}}the last screw of the rack having been turned so often that its purchase crumbled, and it now turned and turned with nothing to '''bite'''{{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|stative|slang}} To [[lack]] [[quality]]; to be [[worthy]] of [[derision]]; to [[suck]].
#: {{ux|en|This music really '''bites'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal|vulgar}} To perform [[oral sex]] on. {{non-gloss|Used in [[invective]]}}.
#: {{ux|en|You don't like that I sat on your car? '''Bite''' me.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|AAVE|slang}} To [[plagiarize]], to [[imitate]].
