===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|en|to gulp}}
From {{inh|en|enm|swolwen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swelgan}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swelgan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swelganą|t=to swallow, revel, devour}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*swelk-|t=to gulp}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|zwelgen|t=to revel, carouse, guzzle}}, {{cog|de|schwelgen|t=to delight, indulge}}, {{cog|da|svælge|t=to swallow, indulge}}, {{cog|nb|svelge|t=to swallow}}, {{cog|nn|svelgje|t=to swallow}}, {{cog|sv|svälja|t=to swallow, gulp}}, {{cog|fo|svølgja|t=to swallow}}, {{cog|is|svelgja|t=to swallow}}, {{cog|ang|swillan}}, {{m|ang|swilian|t=to swill, wash out, gargle}}. See also {{l|en|swill}}.

The noun is from {{inh|en|enm|swolow}}, {{m|enm|swolwe}}, from {{inh|en|ang|swelh}}, {{m|ang|swelg|t=gulf, chasm}} and {{m|ang|ġeswelge|t=gulf, chasm, abyss, whirlpool}}, both from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*swelg}}, {{m|gmw-pro|*swalgi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*swelgaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*swalgiz}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|swiliġe|t=pit}}, {{cog|sco|swelch}}, {{m|sco|swellie}}, {{m|sco|swallie|t=an abyss in the sea, whirlpool}}, {{cog|gml|swelch|t=whirlpool, eddy}}, {{cog|nl|zwelg|t=gorge, chasm, gullet, throat}}, {{cog|non|svelgr|t=whirlpool, current, stream}}.

