==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈweɪ̯st/|[ˈweɪ̯st]}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Naomi Persephone Amethyst (NaomiAmethyst)-waste.wav|a=GA}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-waste.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪst|s=1}}
* {{hyph|en|waste}}
* {{hmp|en|waist<aa:pane-pain>}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|wast}}, {{m|enm|waste|t=a waste|pos=n}}, from {{der|en|xno|-}}, {{der|en|fro-nor|wast}}, {{m|fro|waste|t=a waste}}, from {{der|en|frk|*wōstī|t=a waste}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro||*wōstaz}},<ref>{{R:gem:HGE|*wōstaz|470}}</ref> {{m|gem-pro||*wōstuz}},<ref>{{R:gem:EDPG|head=*wōstu-|page=593|passage=*ueh₂s-tu-}}</ref> from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₁weh₂-|t=empty, wasted}}. Displaced native Middle English {{m|enm|wernen||to refuse}} likely due to the similar sounding {{cog|enm|warnen}}

{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁weh₂-}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{cap|excess}} of material, useless [[by-product]]s{{,}} or [[damaged]], [[unsaleable]] [[product]]s; [[garbage]]; [[rubbish]].
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|date=2 September 2026|author1=Damian O'Neil|author2=Hannah Mitchell|author3=Federica Bendendo|title=Hunt to find 400-tonne waste dump culprits|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/clyejz9l9vdo|journal={{w|BBC News}}|text=Illegal '''waste''' dumped near an airport and weighing an estimated 400 tonnes is being sifted through in an attempt to identify those responsible for it.|accessdate=4 September 2026|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261005132847/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/clyejz9l9vdo|archivedate=5 October 2026}}
# {{cap|excrement}} or [[urine]].
#: {{ux|en|The cage was littered with animal '''waste'''.}}
# A [[wasteland]]; an [[uninhabited]] [[desolate]] [[region]]; a [[wilderness]] or [[desert]].
#* {{RQ:Stevenson Kidnapped|passage=We went down accordingly into the '''waste''', and began to make our toilsome and devious travel towards the eastern verge.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=Edwin Williamson|title=The Penguin history of Latin America|year=1992|publisher=Penguin Books|location=London; New York|isbn=978-0-14-012559-7|page=33|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/isbn_9780140125597/page/33/mode/1up|passage= The pampas of Argentina and the chilly '''wastes''' of Patagonia, like the prairies and deserts of North America, were largely shunned by Spanish settlers until the 1870s.}}
# A place that has been [[lay waste|laid waste]] or [[destroy]]ed.
# A large [[tract]] of [[uncultivated]] land.
# {{lb|en|historical}} The part of the land of a [[manor]] (of whatever size) not used for [[cultivation]] or [[graze|grazing]], nowadays treated as [[common land]].
# A [[vast]] [[expanse]] of [[water]].
# A [[disuse]]d [[mine]] or part of one.
# The action or progress of [[#Verb|wasting]]; [[extravagant]] [[consumption]] or [[ineffectual]] use.
#: {{ux|en|That was a '''waste''' of time!}}
#: {{ux|en|Her life seemed a '''waste'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 March 22|author=Mike Esbester|title=Staff, the public and industry will suffer|journal=RAIL|issue=979|page=39|passage='Rebel railwaymen' at Birmingham New Street refused to wear the new uniforms on the grounds that they were a "complete '''waste''' of public money".}}
# Large [[abundance]] of something, specifically without it being used.
# Gradual [[loss]] or [[decay]].
# A [[decay]]ing of the [[body]] by [[disease]]; [[atrophy]]; [[wasting away]].
# {{lb|en|rare}} {{cap|destruction}} or [[devastation]] caused by [[war]] or [[natural disaster]]s; see "to [[lay waste]]".
# {{lb|en|legal}} A [[cause of action]] which may be brought by the owner of a [[future interest]] in [[property]] against the current owner of that property to prevent the current owner from [[degrade|degrading]] the [[value]] or [[character]] of the property, either intentionally or through [[neglect]].
# {{lb|en|geology}} <!--possibly dated; came from Webster 1913--> Material derived by [[mechanical]] and [[chemical]] [[erosion]] from the land, carried by [[stream]]s to the [[sea]].

