==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|shād}}, {{IPA|en|/ʃeɪd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-shade.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪd|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=noun|:inh|enm:schade|tree=1|text=++}} {{doublet|en|shadow}}. Cognate with {{cog|grc|σκότος}} (whence {{m+|en|scoto-}}) and {{m|grc|σκιά}} (whence {{m+|en|scia-}}, and uncertainly via {{m|grc|σκίουρος}} {{m+|en|squirrel}}).

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} [[darkness|Darkness]] where [[light]], particularly [[sunlight]], is [[block]]ed.
#: {{ux|en|The old oak tree gave '''shade''' in the heat of the day.}}
#: {{ux|en|Temps rose to a sweltering 40 [[degrees Celsius]] in the '''shade'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|chapter=8|passage=Now we plunged into a deep '''shade''' with the boughs lacing each other overhead, and crossed dainty, rustic bridges over the cold trout-streams, the boards giving back the clatter of our horses' feet:{{...}}.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} Something that blocks light, particularly in a [[window]].
#: {{ux|en|Close the '''shade''', please: it's too bright in here.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=March 2023|title=Vitamin D|work=Harvard T.H. Chan School of Public Health|url=https://nutritionsource.hsph.harvard.edu/vitamin-d/|text=Also, people with darker skin tend to have lower blood levels of vitamin D because the pigment (melanin) acts like a '''shade''', reducing production of vitamin D (and also reducing damaging effects of sunlight on skin, including skin cancer).|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261003155600/https://nutritionsource.hsph.harvard.edu/vitamin-d/|archivedate=3 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A variety of a color, in particular one obtained by adding [[black]] (compare [[tint]]).
#: {{ux|en|I've painted my room in five lovely '''shades''' of pink and chartreuse.}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Human Understanding|text=Thus light and colours, as white, red, yellow, blue, with their several degrees or '''shades''', and mixtures, as green, scarlet, purple, sea-green, and the rest, come in only by the eyes{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Lauren Caruso and Jillian Tracy|title=The 22 best sunglasses for summer, according to style experts|url=https://www.cnn.com/cnn-underscored/fashion/best-sunglasses-2023|date=2023-06-26|passage=Speaking of round sunglasses, these lightweight polarized ones and come in two '''shades''' of tortoiseshell as well as black and bronze.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250414045427/https://www.cnn.com/cnn-underscored/fashion/best-sunglasses-2023|archivedate=14 April 2025}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} A [[subtle]] variation in a concept.
#: {{ux|en|'''shades''' of meaning}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1823|author=w:Thomas De Quincey|title=Letters to a Young Man whose Education has been Neglected. No. V. On the English Notices of Kant
|passage=new '''shades''' and combinations of thought}}
#* {{RQ:Macaulay History of England|chapter=3|passage=Every '''shade''' of religious and political opinion had its own headquarters.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|title=Catherine O’Hara Portrayed the Vain and Delusional With a Radical Lack of Vanity|date=Jan 30 2026|author=Judy Berman
|text=These performances, which include plenty of great one-liners and physical gags but also unearth subtler '''shades''' of frustration and self-doubt, are some of my favorites of hers.
|url=https://time.com/7362820/catherine-ohara-obituary/
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260201210725/https://time.com/7362820/catherine-ohara-obituary/}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively|in the plural}} An [[aspect]] that is [[reminiscent]] of something.
#: {{ux|en|'''shades''' of Groucho Marx}}
# A very small [[degree]] of a quantity, or [[variety]] of meaning
#: {{ux|en|That is a '''shade''' too close.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1934|author=w:Agatha Christie|title=Miss Marple Tells a Story
|passage=Mrs. Rhodes who (so I gathered from Mr. Petherick's careful language) was perhaps just a '''shade''' of a hypochondriac, had retired to bed immediately after dinner.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=07 Apr 90|journal=Gay Community News|page=12|author=Wickie Stamps|title=The 'Temple' Is Familiar|text=Five feet in diameter and a '''shade''' above knee high, the center of the fragile white canvass structure is filled with {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly|literary|and|fantasy}} A [[ghost]] or [[specter]]; a [[spirit]].
#: {{ux|en|Too long have I been haunted by that '''shade'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The adventurer was attacked by a '''shade'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|Ceyx and Alcyone
