knife.content:
==English==
[[Image:4Messer (fcm).png|thumb|right|150px|A few kitchen knives: chef's knife, bread knife, steak knife, and paring knife]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|knyfe||noun|obsolete}}
* {{alt|en|knive||verb|uncommon}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|knyf}}, {{m|enm|knif}}, from late {{inh|en|ang|cnīf}}, from {{der|en|non|knífr}} or {{der|en|gmw-pro|*knīb}},<ref>{{R:enm:Gersum|knyf|n.|10182|cat=BB2a}}</ref> from {{der|en|gem-pro|*knībaz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*knīpaną|t=to pinch}}, {{der|en|ine-pro|*gneybʰ-}} (compare {{cog|lt|gnýbti}}, {{m|lt|žnýbti|t=to pinch}}, {{m|lt|gnaibis||pinching}}). Displaced native {{ncog|enm|sax|t=knife}}, from {{ncog|ang|seax}}; and {{ncog|enm|coutel}}, {{m|enm|qwetyll|t=knife}} from {{ncog|fro|coutel}}.

* The verb is {{etydate|1865|nocap=1}}.<ref>{{R:MWO}}</ref> The variant {{m|en|knive}} is {{etydate|1733|nocap=1}}.<!--see entry-->
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|yol|kunnife|t=knife}}, {{cog|frr|knif|t=knife}}, {{cog|nl|knijf|t=long pointy knife, poniard}}, {{cog|de|Knifte|t=rifle; thick slicebread}}, {{cog|nds-de|Knief|t=knife}}, {{cog|lb|Knäip|t=paring knife}}, {{cog|da,nb,nn|kniv|t=knife}}, {{cog|fo|knívur|t=knife}}, {{cog|is|hnífur}}, {{m|is|knífur|t=knife}}, {{cog|sv|knif}}, {{m|sv|kniv|t=knife}}.
{{col-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnaɪ̯f/|a=RP,GA}}
** {{audio|en|En-uk-a knife.ogg|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|En-us-knife.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɐɪ̯f/|/ˈnɜɪ̯f/|/ˈnʌɪ̯f/|/ˈnəɪ̯f/|a=CA,Canadian raising}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnɑɪ̯f/|/ˈnɒ̈ɪ̯f/|a=AU,NZ}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈnaːf/|a=[[w:Southern accent (United States)|Inland Southern US]],ZA,[[w:Monophthongization|/aɪ̯/-ungliding]]}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪf|s=1}}
* {{hyph|en|knife}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|knives}}

# {{senseid|en|Q32489}}A [[utensil]] or a [[tool]] designed for cutting, consisting of a flat piece of hard material, usually steel or other metal (the [[blade]]), usually [[sharpen]]ed on one edge, attached to a [[handle]]. The blade may be pointed for piercing.
#: {{ux|en|He was looking for a '''knife''' to chop some steak.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Scott Smith|title=The Ruins|page=273
|passage=Jeff was bent low over the backboard, working with the '''knife''', a steady sawing motion, his shirt soaked through with sweat.}}
# A [[weapon]] designed with the aforementioned specifications intended for [[slash]]ing or [[stab]]bing but too short to be called a [[sword]]; a [[dagger]].
# Any blade-like part in a tool or a machine designed for cutting, such as that of a [[chipper]].

