splash.content:
==English==
{{wp}}
[[Image:2006-02-13_Drop-impact.jpg|thumb|right|A splash.]]
{{rf-sound example}}

===Etymology===
Probably an alteration of {{m|en|plash}} (compare {{m|en|spatter}}, {{m|en|spill}} for the initial ''s-'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/splæʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-splash.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|æʃ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|onomatopoeia}} The sound made by an object hitting a [[liquid]].
#: {{ux|en|I heard a '''splash''' when the rock landed in the pond.}}
# A small amount of liquid.
#: {{ux|en|I felt a '''splash''' of rain, so I put up my hood.}}
#: {{ux|en|I felt a '''splash''' of water on my leg as the car drove into the nearby puddle.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|passage=Add the tomato purée and cook for a further 4-5 minutes. Add a '''splash''' of whisky to the pan, scraping up any browned bits from the bottom of the pan with a wooden spoon to deglaze.|url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/food/recipes/grilledfilletofhalib_92475|title=recipe, Grilled fillet of halibut and langoustine tails with smoked haddock risotto and shellfish froth|author=Chris Morrison|accessdate=17 August 2014|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20121027024152/http://www.bbc.co.uk:80/food/recipes/grilledfilletofhalib_92475|archivedate=27 October 2012}}
# A small amount (of color).
#: {{ux|en|The painter put a '''splash''' of blue on the wall to make it more colorful}}
# A mark or stain made from a small amount of liquid.
#: {{ux|en|There was a visible '''splash''' on his pants after he went to the bathroom.}}
# An [[impact]] or [[impression]].
#: {{ux|en|The new movie made quite a '''splash''' upon its release.}}
# {{lb|en|computing|informal}} A [[splash screen]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Ron Carswell; Heidi Webb|title=Guide to Microsoft Virtual PC 2007 and Virtual Server 2005
|passage=When the '''splash''' appears with Please wait, wait for Windows to start configuration.}}
# {{lb|en|wrestling}} A [[body press]]; a move where the wrestler jumps forward from a raised platform such as the top [[turnbuckle]], landing [[stomach]] first across an opponent lying on the ground below.
# {{lb|en|dated}} A [[cosmetic]] [[powder]] to [[whiten]] the [[complexion]].
# {{lb|en|journalism}} A large, [[prominent]] [[headline]] or [[article]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Bob Franklin|title=Local Journalism and Local Media: Making the Local News
|passage=So for a local newspaper, a '''splash''' on a fatal crash is just the first of a series of reports.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Victoria Hoffarth|title=When Turtles Come Home|page=69
|passage=After the brouhaha and the newspaper headline '''splashes''', each of these contentious items would simply die its own quiet death to be replaced by a newer scandal: {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|comics}} A [[splash page]].
# {{lb|en|military|slang}} The shooting down of an aircraft over water.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Robin L. Rielly|title=Kamikaze Attacks of World War II|page=267
|passage=Hits were observed, but again the poor functioning of VT ammunition hindered in effecting a '''splash'''.}}
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} The [[bleeding]] caused by a [[knife]] [[wound]].
#* {{quote-song|en|lyricist=Td of TPL|title=Stop Check|url=https://genius.com/Tpl-stop-check-lyrics|date=2020-07-02|note=1:52–1:56|passage=Jojo caught up and gave him a '''splash'''<br/>Slap that wap, get rid of them plats}}
# {{lb|en|MLE|slang}} A [[knife]].
#: {{syn|en|splasher|[[jooka]] ~ [[jooker]]|nank|shank|bassy|rambo|pokey|chete|ying}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=#CO CMoney|title=Don’t Ask|date=13-08-2021|note=2:51–2:53|passage=You grip your '''splash''' for fashion—me and you, we ain’t got the same intentions.}}

