===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[hit]] or [[agitate]] [[liquid]] so that [[part]] of it [[separate]]s from the [[principal]] [[liquid]] [[mass]].
#: {{ux|en|sit and '''splash''' in the bathtub}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=October 28 1990|author=w:Paul Simon|chapter=She Moves On|title=w:The Rhythm of the Saints|publisher=Warner Bros.
|passage=I know the reason I feel so blessed / My heart still '''splashes''' inside my chest}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} {{q|of a liquid}} To disperse suddenly as a result of an impulse; to [[splatter]].
#: {{ux|en|Water '''splashed''' everywhere.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hit]] or [[agitate]] (liquid) so that [[part]] of it [[separate]]s from the [[principal]] [[liquid]] [[mass]].
#: {{uxi|en|She '''splashed''' water onto her face.}}
#: {{uxi|en|I accidentally '''splashed''' some coffee on my keyboard.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hit]] or [[expel]] [[liquid]] at.
#: {{ux|en|The children were '''splashing''' each other playfully in the sea.}}
#: {{ux|en|When she comes in the door, '''splash''' her with perfume.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To create an [[impact]] or [[impression]]; to [[print]], [[post]]{{,}} or [[publicize]] [[prominent]]ly.
#: {{ux|en|The headline was '''splashed''' across newspapers everywhere.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=8 Apr 78|journal=Gay Community News|page=5|author=Eric Rogers|title=Speaking Out|text=The March 5, 1978 issue of ''National Reader'' {{...}} contained an exciting front page headline -- "Most Major Hollywood Stars Are Gay or Bisexual!!!!" '''Splashed''' on the cover are photos of Rock Hudson, Shaun and David Cassidy, {{...}} and, last but not least, Lily Tomlin.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:Taylor Swift|title=The Lucky One|album=w:Red (Taylor's Version)|year=2012|year_published=2021|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4LtQxA_ooLk|text=Now it's big black cars and Riviera views / And your lover in the foyer doesn't even know you / And your secrets end up '''splashed''' on the news front page}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[spend]] (money).
#: {{ux|en|After pay day I can afford to '''splash''' some cash and buy myself a motorbike.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[roughly]] [[fill]] with [[color]].
#* {{quote-web|en|date=July 6 2021|work=BBC Sport|author=w:Phil McNulty|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/57743513|title=Italy beat Spain on penalties: 'Pure theatre as Italy present formidable obstacle in final'|passage=This was pure theatre, with a 60,000 crowd at Wembley adding colour to the fight to face either England or Denmark in Sunday's final, the stadium '''splashed''' with the red of Spain at one end and the victorious blue of Italy at the other as crowds flocked back in ever bigger numbers after pandemic restrictions were lifted.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240927223738/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/57743513|archivedate=27 September 2024}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|nautical}} To [[launch]] a ship.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1999|author=David M. Kennedy|journal="Victory at Sea": Atlantic Monthly|month=March
|passage=In the two years following Midway, Japanese shipyards managed to '''splash''' only six additional fleet carriers. The United States in the same period added seventeen, along with ten medium carriers and eighty-six escort carriers.}}
# {{lb|en|military|slang}} To [[shoot down]] (an [[aircraft]]) over [[water]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Robin L. Rielly|title=Kamikaze Attacks of World War II|page=234
|passage=Planes were sighted at about 5000 yards, fire was opened at 4500 yards; the first plane was '''splashed''' about 1800 yards from the ship, the second was '''splashed''' about 3000 yards from the ship and rudder shifted to hard right.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|MLE}} To [[stab]] (a person), causing them to [[bleed]].
#: {{syn|en|chef|ching|Thesaurus:stab}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=18-10-2017|lyricist=Knockoutned|artist=#Moscow17 Ruth x Knockoutned|title=Panic|passage=Grab him, don't panic, rambo under my jacket<br/>Nap him, '''splash''' him, then I'm petrol bath my jacket}}

